const users = new UserRepository();

export function listActiveUsers() {
  return users.findActive();
}

export function findUser(id) {
  return users.findById(id);
}

export function softDeleteUser(id, when) {
  return users.softDelete(id, when);
}
```

**`tests/user-service.test.js`**: turn the two tests into `async` tests that `await` the functions instead of using `done` callbacks.

**`src/api/routes.js:8-9`**: the migration steps don't mention this file, but it needs a change. The `/users` and `/users/:id` handlers pass a callback to `listActiveUsers` and `findUser`. Once those return promises, the callback is never called, so both endpoints would hang without raising any error. I'd adapt the two handlers so they still hand results to the callback:
```js
handler: (req, cb) => listActiveUsers().then((r) => cb(null, r), cb)
handler: (req, cb) => findUser(Number(req.params.id)).then((r) => cb(null, r), cb)
```
No other code calls `softDeleteUser`.

After that I'll run `node --test tests/user-service.test.js`. To go ahead, approve the writes when prompted or add allow rules for these paths and `node --test`, then tell me to retry.

